---
title: Tensors and backends
summary: skoro-backend, the foundation. The sealed Backend trait over burn, the batched shape conventions for points, tangent vectors and frames, and the precision policy.
order: 1
---

Everything in skoro eventually becomes a burn `Tensor`. `skoro-backend` fixes *which* backends
are allowed and *what shape* each kind of tensor has.

## Supported backends

`Backend` is a subtrait of burn's backend trait, sealed so that only the backends skoro has been
verified against implement it: `Flex` (CPU) and `CubeBackend` (GPU via cubecl). None of burn's
autodiff backends are among them. Skoro differentiates on its own (see
[Differentiable operations](../operations/)).

```
{../../../../crates/skoro-backend/src/lib.rs:17..32}
```

## Shape conventions

Types are aliases over `Tensor` whose names carry meaning. Every one of them is **batched**:
axis 0 indexes independent problems.

```
{../../../../crates/skoro-backend/src/lib.rs:60..93}
```

Two sizes appear throughout the library, and they are different whenever a quantity is curved:

| Quantity | storage | dimension |
| --- | ---: | ---: |
| `Real` | 1 | 1 |
| `Euclidean<3>` | 3 | 3 |
| `SO3` | 9 | 3 |
| `SE3` | 12 | 6 |

Points use storage size; tangent vectors, cotangents, gradients and Jacobian columns use
dimension. A *frame* is a stack of vectors, `[batch, dimension, frame]`, which is how many
derivative directions travel through a pass at once.

## Precision

The float policy is process-wide and locked on first use. See
[Backends and precision](../../guide/backends-and-precision/) and
[Precision is a lock-once policy](../../design/precision-policy/).

